comments.text:
Read-only design: durable partial assessment checkpoint increment.

Decision: retain the existing immutable milestone/workbook model. Each existing ten-score assessment progress boundary additionally commits one JSON Task attachment; it never creates a workbook, ReportBlock, or scorecard-artifact revision. The Report parameter pointer is the only commit point, so interrupted uploads are orphaned and ignored.

Attachment contract assessment_batch_checkpoint.v1:
- identity: run_key, account_id, procedure_task_id, report_id;
- frozen binding: canonical run_spec_sha256, rank_packet_sha256, rank_evidence_fingerprint, ranking_revision;
- contiguous batch: sequence (one-based), prior_sequence, prior_payload_sha256, total_ranked, start_index, end_index, ordered target_refs, and the exact assessment packets;
- integrity: canonical JSON bytes uploaded through existing TASK_ATTACHMENT tickets; descriptor carries object_key, content_type, size_bytes, sha256, task_id, source_revision, and a generated immutable filename.

Report metadata stores only assessment_checkpoint_latest: schema/kind plus the latest verified attachment descriptor and identity/binding fields. Each payload points to the prior descriptor/checksum, forming a contiguous immutable chain. No inline assessment rows, no new GraphQL resources, no ReportBlock change, and no new workbook revision.

State machine:
1. Ranking milestone is fully committed.
2. Assessment computes up to ten rows in memory.
3. Upload and optional read-back verify one immutable JSON attachment; attach it to the existing Task.
4. Conditionally advance the Report metadata pointer only if it still names the expected prior sequence/checksum. Then publish existing live progress. If either pointer or progress publication fails, stop retryably; never assess beyond the last committed batch.
5. On resume, load the normal ranking checkpoint, then follow assessment_checkpoint_latest backwards through attachment descriptors. Verify attachment checksums and contiguous chain before restoring rows. Resume at end_index plus one. A completed final partial batch is reused to publish the normal assessment milestone rather than recomputed.
6. Once the normal assessment milestone commits, the chain remains historical evidence but is no longer an active resume source.

Recovery validation (fail closed with OptimizationRunIntegrityError): payload and descriptor must match current Task ID, Report ID, account, run_key, canonical frozen run spec, ranking revision, full rank-packet SHA, rank evidence fingerprint, sequence/previous-sequence/previous-payload digest, exact ranked target order, exact row count and index range. Missing/malformed/reordered/duplicate/out-of-range rows, skipped sequence, mismatched predecessor, changed rank/spec/account/task/report, or checksum failure are integrity failures. Ticket/auth/read failures are retryable publication errors and preserve the active attempt.

Runner integration: before assessment, ask the report service for a validated partial checkpoint bound to the loaded ranking packet; initialize assessment_rows and loop index from it. After each current ten-row boundary, call append_assessment_batch before publish_progress. Do not change ranking, diagnosis, optimizer dispatch, or promotion semantics.

Outside-in tests:
- ten-row and final-short batches persist immutable TASK_ATTACHMENT JSON with read-back checksum and no added workbook/milestone revision;
- recovery restores a two-batch chain and calls assess only on remaining exact ranked targets;
- interruption after commit but before progress resumes without duplicate assessment;
- interruption before pointer commit ignores orphan upload and safely reruns only that uncommitted batch;
- reject altered run/account/task/report/spec/rank revision/rank fingerprint, checksum, target order, duplicate/missing target, gap/reordered sequence, wrong predecessor, malformed descriptor, and stale concurrent pointer;
- ticket/authority failure remains retryable and leaves prior chain usable;
- full final assessment milestone supersedes the chain as active resume state.

Minimal production files: plexus/optimization/run_report.py (checkpoint descriptor, attachment commit/load/verification); plexus/optimization/portfolio_run.py (batch-boundary persistence and resume cursor). Test files: corresponding run_report_test.py and portfolio_run_test.py; update only any runtime test doubles whose strict report-service contract must expose the two methods. No code edited in this design pass.
